            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the inpatient treatment of your patient, a 74-year-old male, admitted on 24/04/2026 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Physical examination, pulse oximetry, arterial blood gas analysis, chest X-ray, and blood tests were performed, confirming an acute exacerbation without evidence of pneumonia or cardiac decompensation. The patient was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive intravenous fluids. Monitoring of vital signs was performed throughout the stay. The patient recovered satisfactorily and was discharged in stable condition on 25/04/2026. I recommend continuation of his regular inhaler regimen and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
